es, provides economic, financial, and management consulting services worldwide. It advises clients on economic and financial matters pertaining to litigation and regulatory proceedings; and guide corporations through business strategy and performance-related issues. The company also offers consulting services, including research and analysis, expert testimony, and comprehensive support in litigation and regulatory proceedings in the areas of finance, accounting, economics, insurance, and forensic accounting and investigations to corporate clients and attorneys. In addition, it provides management consulting services, such as strategy development, performance improvement, corporate strategy and portfolio analysis, estimation of market demand, environmental, social and corporate governance and sustainability strategy and analysis, design and implementation of auction and bidding, new product pricing strategies, survey and market research, valuation of intellectual property and other assets, assessment of competitors' actions, and analysis of new sources of supply. The company serves various industries comprising blockchain and cryptocurrency; communications and media; consumer, health, and wellness products; energy; entertainment and leisure; financial services; healthcare; life sciences; manufacturing and industries; natural resources; retail and distribution; technology; and transportation. The company was incorporated in 1965 and is headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Paul A. Maleh | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 61 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $731K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $18K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["CRA International,Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.4B market cap on $752M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 28% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 20-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 32%.","The business throws off $19M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.41\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 16\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 4.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 81% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8135740408261934},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Did CRA International (NASDAQ:CRAI) Reach Higher Revenue Guidance?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/smallcap/how-did-cra-international-nasdaqcrai-reach-higher-revenue-guidance","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795698360.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.026,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"CRAI Stock Surges 51% in 6 Months: Here's What Investors Should Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3034726/crai-stock-surges-51-in-6-months-here-s-what-investors-should-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cprice_surge_%2F_plunge-3034726","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795537200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CRA International (CRAI) is a Top-Ranked Momentum Stock: Should You Buy?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3033853/cra-international-crai-is-a-top-ranked-momentum-stock-should-you-buy?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_momentum_score-3033853","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp"